 ## Temporary Framework-Default Overrides Needed for Rollback
 
-### In This Release (while rollback to Rails 7.0 remains possible)
-
-1. **`config.active_support.cache_format_version = 7.0`** (`config/application.rb`):
-   - Overrides `7.2` defaults (`7.1`) because Rails 7.0 cannot deserialize `7.1` cache entries. Safe to remove in the next Rails 8.1 release once rollback to Rails 7.0 is retired (this Rails 7.2 release can read `7.1` cache entries on rollback from Rails 8.1).
-2. **`config.action_dispatch.cookies_serializer = :hybrid`** (`config/application.rb`):
-   - Temporarily overrides `7.2` defaults (`:json`) so any unrefreshed Marshal session cookies are still read and rotated to JSON (writes JSON readable by Rails 7.0, 7.2, and 8.1). Retire in the next Rails 8.1 release (`:json`).
-3. **`SHA1` KeyGenerator rotations in `config/initializers/upgrade_compatibility.rb`**:
-   - Keeps any surviving `SHA1`-derived session cookies or 30-day `:mail_links` tokens from pre-7.0 deploys valid while `SHA256` is active. Retire in the next Rails 8.1 release once Rails 7.0 rollback is retired and the 30-day TTL + session lifetime have elapsed.
+None. All temporary rollback overrides (`cache_format_version = 7.0`,
+`cookies_serializer = :hybrid`, and `config/initializers/upgrade_compatibility.rb`)
+have been retired. Only the permanent Redmine override
